# Monorepo note

Root `railway.toml` was removed so GitHub deploys do not force one Dockerfile on both services.
Set Dockerfile path **per service** in the Railway dashboard:

| Service | Dockerfile |
|---------|------------|
| `procharacters-api` | `backend/Dockerfile` |
| `procharacters-web` | `frontend/Dockerfile` |

**Do not** use the repo-root `Dockerfile` for either product service.
That file builds the optional Python **WebRTC + trainer** side service (`app/`).
Local only (or a deliberate third Railway service):

```bash
docker compose --profile webrtc up --build webrtc
```

See [docs/DEPLOY.md](./docs/DEPLOY.md) and [docs/WEBRTC-ENGINE.md](./docs/WEBRTC-ENGINE.md).
